cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GenoDiplo, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "GenoDiplo: a Snakemake workflow for diplomonad genome assembly and annotation"
abstract: >-
  GenoDiplo is a Snakemake workflow that takes raw long-read sequencing data
  through assembly, quality evaluation, and structural and functional
  annotation of diplomonad genomes. It was developed for the reference genome
  of Hexamita inflata and applied in simplified form to the draft genome of
  Spironucleus barkhanus.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Zeynep
    family-names: Akdeniz
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5279-6077"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zeyak/GenoDiplo"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
keywords:
  - genome assembly
  - genome annotation
  - Snakemake
  - diplomonads
  - comparative genomics
